{"result":"{
  "id": "17902",
  "key": "SFCC-52",
  "summary": "Global Header UI",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/17902",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n**I want** to see a consistent global header on every page, \n**so that** I can always access key navigation and account features regardless of where I am on the site.\n\nReference image (Figma is leading):\n\n![\"image-20260618-040938.png\"](image-20260618-040938.png)\n\n----\n\nThe global header is a sticky component displayed at the top of every page across all storefronts and devices. It contains the Zimmermann logo, header icons. The header remains visible as the shopper scrolls down the page.\n\nThis story covers the **header shell and layout only** — the visual structure, component placement, and sticky behaviour. Icon destinations (Search, Account, Wish List, Cart) are wired up as the underlying pages and features are built in their respective stories. The exception is the logo (links to homepage).\n\n**Header elements:**\n\n  - **Zimmermann logo/wordmark* — left aligned with and below the top categories in the header, links back to the homepage on click\n  - **Navigation menu -* based on the latest Figma design, left-aligned top-level categories include: NEW, CLOTHING, ACCESSORIES, COLLECTIONS, Z.IMMERSE. For this user story, we will set up the first basis of the navigation items in SFCC.\n  - **Header icons (right-aligned):* Search, Account, Bag, Wishlist, Bag; displayed as visual elements - destination page in other stories.\n\n**Responsive behaviour:** There is a header design for both desktop and mobile.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Blocked",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "Medium"
  },
  "assignee": {
    "display_name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
    "name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
    "email": "marcel.a.n.navarro@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/482e2e100517026f4980d6455214aa11?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMN-6.png"
  },
  "reporter": {
    "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
  },
  "labels": [
    "DesignDependent",
    "HPC-015",
    "HPC-016",
    "HPC-018",
    "HPC-019",
    "HPC-020",
    "HPC-021",
    "HPC-026",
    "HPC-027"
  ],
  "created": "2026-06-18T11:45:13.950+1000",
  "updated": "2026-07-28T10:35:43.659+1000",
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13525",
      "body": "Hey User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d , I had review of this card and a little bit like the story we reviewed last week, here are my thoughts on a few changes to the Acceptance Criteria section:\n\n  - **Desktop & Mobile*\n      - I think 5 & 6 belong with the Cart user story\n        - With the Cart, is there any designs on what happens if they click on the cart? If so, that Design would also be part of the Cart user story. \n  - **Mobile*\n      - I think 8 - 11 should be placed in the Navigation user story as that’s behaviour we need to build into the nav CSS & JS\n\nHopefully not too much work to move around, but happy to have a call and discuss as well. \n\nThanks Jas!",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-26T08:08:00.911+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-26T08:08:00.911+1000"
    }
  ]
}"}

