  "key": "SFCC-91",
  "summary": "PDP UI — Colour Swatches & Variation Selection",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18129",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper,\n\n**I want** to see all available colours for a product and be able to switch between them on the page,\n\n**so that** I can explore the full range of colour options before choosing which to buy.\n\n----\n\nImage for reference (final design in Figma is leading):\n\n![\"image-20260701-114754.png\"](image-20260701-114754.png)\n\nThis story covers the rendering of colour swatches on the PDP and the interaction logic when a shopper selects a different colour. Swatches are driven by the index image — one product image per colour variation that is designated in SFCC BM as the representative swatch image.\n\nMost products do not have a wide range of colours available, however, Dani confirmed max needed number of colours will likely be around **7.** \n\nHere’s a current product that has 4 colours:[Lumi Sandal Lilac Online ]( Zimmermann|https://www.zimmermann.com/shoes/flats-sneakers/lumi-sandal-lilac.html)",
